{"seq":18,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/zero-lean-mcp-instructions-opus-gbrain-mu-v03-dev2/sy-02-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T08:08:44.389Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"89ba4dca7c87f953de3f288d234b9073fe374d3d915c4d13ae90cf70f88c7485","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"Here are the Marrow Fieldworks ticket numbers I found:\n\n*From Moss's notes* (\"Moss: Central handoffs next week\", 2 Jan 2026)\n• *#4409*: recurring timeout on the Gatehouse Check-In report at the Salina North yard (Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron, 06:00 flatbed intake)\n• *#4412*: driver SMS prompt glitch when staging combine trailers on unpaved overflow lots\nHollis flagged both as open before the 5 Jan handoff.\n\n*From #central-random* (your message, 13 Oct, 09:27)\n• *#8841*: West yard Door 2 double-booking when flatbeds check in early at the kiosk (Plains depots, tractor-bay alerts)\n\nOne caveat: neither source names Marrow Fieldworks next to the ticket numbers. The Moss note says Marrow Fieldworks changes hands on 5 Jan and lists those two tickets under \"Pree's dealer account\". The #central-random thread calls it \"Tobias's dealer account\". I'm treating the dealer account as Marrow Fieldworks, so please check that's right.\n\nI left these out because they belong to other accounts: FR-882 (Marrow Agrisupply, a different account) and #88412 (Tansleigh Packaging). Moss's other Central note, the cheat sheet, has no ticket numbers. The notes don't say whether #4409 and #4412 were ever closed, so check their status before the call."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
{"seq":19,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/zero-lean-mcp-instructions-opus-gbrain-mu-v03-dev2/sy-02-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T08:08:49.288Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"31d0f6a09332129bbbaaf19ab81323eeca715b4a3324177786b2bc44373dd760","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I found three ticket numbers that look like Marrow Fieldworks and sent you the list in our DM:\n\n**From Moss's notes** (\"Moss: Central handoffs next week\", 2 Jan 2026). Hollis flagged both as open before the 5 Jan handoff:\n- **#4409:** a timeout that keeps coming back on the Gatehouse Check-In report at the Salina North yard. It hits Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron during the 06:00 flatbed intake.\n- **#4412:** a driver SMS prompt glitch when combine trailers are staged on unpaved overflow lots.\n\n**From #central-random** (your message, 13 Oct, 09:27):\n- **#8841:** West yard Door 2 at the Plains depots double-books when flatbeds check in early at the kiosk. You raised it while checking the tractor-bay alerts.\n\n- **Please confirm the account:** neither source puts the name Marrow Fieldworks next to a ticket number. The Moss note says Marrow Fieldworks changes hands on 5 Jan, and lists the two tickets under \"Pree's dealer account\". The #central-random thread calls it \"Tobias's dealer account\". I'm assuming the dealer account is Marrow Fieldworks.\n- **Left out:** FR-882 is a Marrow Agrisupply request, which is a different account. #88412 is Tansleigh Packaging.\n- **Other Moss notes:** his Central cheat sheet has no ticket numbers.\n- **Status:** the notes don't say whether #4409 and #4412 were ever closed, so check before the call."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
